description: Map layers with PostGIS geometry must ship as Mapbox Vector Tiles (MVT)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Vector tiles for map layers

New (and converted) map **render** layers whose geometry lives in PostGIS must be served as Mapbox Vector Tiles, not as a whole-network GeoJSON download.

## Backend

- Add a `*TileService` that builds one tile with the shared bounds pattern (`ST_TileEnvelope` → filter `geom && wgs` → `ST_AsMVTGeom` → `ST_AsMVT`).
- Add a `*TileController` at `GET /api/<resource>/tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}.mvt`.
- Reuse `app.tile.extent`, `app.tile.buffer`, and `app.tile.max-zoom` (see existing `RoadTileService`, `SegmentTileService`, `FullNetworkTileService`).
- Keep `/geojson` only when needed for analysis, import, or a documented exception (e.g. FWD chainage stretch). Say why in a comment if you leave a layer on GeoJSON.

## Frontend

- When `TILES_ON` (default; opt out with `?tiles=0`), register `type: 'vector'` with `tiles: [...]` and set `source-layer` to the MVT layer name.
- Do not preload a full FeatureCollection just to paint the map.
- Flatten free-form jsonb attrs as a text property (`props_json` / `attrs_json`) and merge on click, matching assets and Full Road Network.

## Known GeoJSON holdouts (do not "fix" without a real tiling design)

- FWD map layer is MVT (`/api/assets/fwd/tiles/...`); keep `/geojson` only for inspector/HUD chainage lookup
- Traffic stations (linear reference; small payload — GeoJSON is fine)
- District / constituency boundaries (small overlays)
- Ephemeral UI sources (`sel-road`, measure)
